# Deploy website crawler (Azure)

When the user asks to **deploy** the website crawler (or “push to ACR”, “release crawler”, “deploy web app”), do this:

1. **Confirm one-time setup** (do not paste secret values into chat): GitHub Actions secrets `AZURE_CLIENT_ID`, `AZURE_TENANT_ID`, `AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID` and variables `ACR_NAME`, `IMAGE_REPOSITORY`, `AZURE_RESOURCE_GROUP`, `AZURE_WEBAPP_NAME` — see `docs/DEPLOY-AZURE.md`.

2. **Preferred: run the workflow** from the **repository root** (`gpta-website-crawler`), default branch `main` unless they specify otherwise:

   ```bash
   gh workflow run deploy-acr-webapp.yml --ref main
   ```

   Optional custom image tag:

   ```bash
   gh workflow run deploy-acr-webapp.yml --ref main -f image_tag=<tag>
   ```

3. If `gh` is not available or not authenticated, tell them to use **GitHub → Actions → “Deploy crawler (ACR + Web App)” → Run workflow**.

4. After a successful deploy, remind them to set GPTA **`WEBSITE_CRAWLER_URL`** to `https://<AZURE_WEBAPP_NAME>.azurewebsites.net/scrape` (replace with their real app host if custom domain).

Do **not** re-run a deploy if a workflow is already in progress unless the user explicitly asks to retry or cancel.
